{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man","id":1482405,"title":"Thoughts about The Bloody Man","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-30T14:35:45-07:00","id":1482405,"title":"Thoughts about The Bloody Man","content":"This legend is fascinating, to think that Vampirism's born from the weaver and corrupted by the wyrm's blood<br /> It seems that the weaver power gave vampires their immortality and Disciplines. The Wyrm's blood seems to be the beast which devour the vampire soul and make him fall to savagery.<br /> <br /> So many questions about the lore could be asked, like if the weaver gift another being without wyrms interventions, could that create a uncorrupted vampirism? The ananasi's use blood pool and are direct creations of the weaver after all<br /> Could a fera be gifted that way and become full hybrid?<br /> What would be a gift from the wyld itself or the wyrm ?<br /> If a vampire get to golconda is he &quot;free&quot; from the wyrm influence and obtain true vampirism?<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T04:20:42-07:00","id":1482475,"title":"","content":"The legends of Kindred and Garou diverge. Both try to understand the other supernatural, but don't want to jump out from their own shoes. If you take the Gehenna scenarios as valid, the judeo-christian vampire creation myth is the correct one.<br /> <br /> About a perfect vamp: Check the Posessed book. There a perfected (from the standpoint of Gradma Wyver) version of vampires are described.<br /> <br /> Abominations are already &quot;full-hybrid&quot;.<br /> <br /> Gift of the Wyrm or Wyld? I can't really understand the question. But they don't really give gifts.<br /> <br /> Golconda is not freedom, but a consciously maintained state of inner pace - as far as I see it. If the tenets are violated, it's lost for ever. And every vampire is a true vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:25:52-07:00","id":1482514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482475#post1482475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The legends of Kindred and Garou diverge. Both try to understand the other supernatural, but don't want to jump out from their own shoes. If you take the Gehenna scenarios as valid, the judeo-christian vampire creation myth is the correct one.</div> </div> </div> </div>As always it depend on what the ST decide is the true version or if he will invent a new story that connect everything<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482475#post1482475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominations are already &quot;full-hybrid&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no, by real hybrid i mean a fera that do not lose his healing factor, his connection with Ga\u00efa and his sanity in the process<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482475#post1482475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Gift of the Wyrm or Wyld? I can't really understand the question. But they don't really give gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to that legend the weaver took a human and made him immortal. You can see this as a benediction (or curse) granted by the weaver itself, so if the wyld, the wyrm or even Ga\u00efa do the same on a being what kind of benediction/curse would it be? (This is not a real question i'm asking to someone, just some reflexions)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482475#post1482475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Golconda is not freedom, but a consciously maintained state of inner pace - as far as I see it. If the tenets are violated, it's lost for ever. And every vampire is a true vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what i know Golconda free the vampire from his beast and allow him to access every Disciplines powers he has without generation limit the only thing that remain the same is his blood pool and his blood spend per round. So if the beast is somehow the Wyrm influence then that free the vampire from it<br /> <br /> All this thoughts are just reflexion i wanted to share, not true questions about the lore or game rules. I'm just fascinated by the views of each race about the other","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:45:24-07:00","id":1482519,"title":"","content":"IMO, bad idea to mush-up Garou and Kindred. Vampires outclass Garou by a huge margin. TOO huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:15:41-07:00","id":1482537,"title":"","content":"The Bloody Man was someone's attempt at creating an in-setting legend of the Garou to account for vampires. But I don't think it's a very good one so I don't use it. <br /> <br /> The Triat are supposed to be several degrees removed from the fiddly bits of creation. They are anthropomorphized entities of metaphysical principles. I would have preferred a legend/myth that attributed it to one of the Bane Incarnas (and perhaps certain patronizing or curses by the Celestines) and left any reference to the Triat to the speculations of Garou theologians and lorekeepers. So in the chronicles I ST I replaced this with a legend I like better for the Garou (and of course, certain Garou occult experts have their own ideas that don't align with the popular myth known to most Garou).<br /> <br /> The advantage of the Garou perspective is that they are a third party with advanced understanding of the Umbra and its metaphysics. The disadvantage is that the Garou have their own biases and vastly incomplete knowledge on vampires. Ideally the Garou should have some kind of insight, but be wildly off because of their own ignorance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T14:47:32-07:00","id":1482541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482519#post1482519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires outclass Garou by a huge margin. TOO huge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are way more powerfull than Garou i agree... but Garou are way more dangerous than the more powerfull of them.<br /> According to the lore a lone garou defeated Set, a clan founder.<br /> Thanks to the spirits and their infinite variety of gift they can teach to garou, a werewolf can learn (of course with time and merit) a large variety of powers allowing them to do almost anything they want<br /> Silent striders have gift that allow them to disable every blood power including vampires disciplines and blood ability. A silver fang gift allow them to completely desintegrate a vampire without needing to touch him<br /> <br /> In a scenario where the first vampire would face a legendary werewolf with the more powerfull gifts possible, the first vampire would be completely overwhelmed by the efficiency of the Legendary werewolf. <br /> But in classical scenario a very old and low generation vampire could easily erase a standart pack (and would be tracked by another well prepared to face him next)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-31-2022, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T19:07:58-07:00","id":1482561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482514#post1482514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no, by real hybrid i mean a fera that do not lose his healing factor, his connection with Ga\u00efa and his sanity in the process</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically possible, but not for abominations.<br /> <br /> Vampire Fomori are able to gain all of the benefits of being fera (regeneration, rage, gnosis that doesn't deplete over time, and ability to learn gifts included), and fomori even have fomori-exclusive abilities that allow them to reproduce, gain immense amounts of xp Very quickly, and even evolve to gain new abilities without losing autonomy or gaining taints. Being fomori, they Don't gain any of the penalties of Abominations and Vampires even gain less drawbacks compared to other fomori as long as it isn't a bane of blood or madness(reference freaks legion, possessed, and w20 book of the wyrm).<br /> <br /> Granted, said vampire-fomori hybrid is basically an infernalist enemy hunted by all vampire And fera alike... but that isn't really different from abominations. Basically Vamp-Fomori outclass Abominations in every considerable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T23:01:28-07:00","id":1482576,"title":"","content":"Some of those crasy fomory powers were nerferd (fortunately) in W20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T04:40:28-07:00","id":1482590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482576#post1482576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of those crasy fomory powers were nerferd (fortunately) in W20.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think the fomori rules in W20 are updates to Possessed and Freaks Legion for the same reason I wouldn't consider the rules for vampires in the same book to be an update for V20, they seem more like plug-and-play rules to make it easy for the ST to throw NPCs at the players.<br /> <br /> They don't have any of the mechanics for play or unique backgrounds, merits and advantages found in the mentioned books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T09:23:00-07:00","id":1482610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482561#post1482561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire Fomori are able to gain all of the benefits of being fera (regeneration, rage, gnosis that doesn't deplete over time, and ability to learn gifts included), and fomori even have fomori-exclusive abilities that allow them to reproduce, gain immense amounts of xp Very quickly, and even evolve to gain new abilities without losing autonomy or gaining taints. Being fomori, they Don't gain any of the penalties of Abominations and Vampires even gain less drawbacks compared to other fomori as long as it isn't a bane of blood or madness(reference freaks legion, possessed, and w20 book of the wyrm).</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean a vampire that would be possessed by a wolf spirit?<br /> And another thing is that in the Umbra everything can be real as long as there is a counterpart in the physical world, so do you think there could be vampire spirits? They would probably be banes but is it something possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T09:43:48-07:00","id":1482611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482610#post1482610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean a vampire that would be possessed by a wolf spirit?</div> </div> </div> </div>No... er, mostly. Wolf spirits would be more Gaian than anything. The wyrm is the spiritual god of decay, destruction, and corruption, so spirits aligned to it would be things like fungi and parasites instead of normal plant/animal spirits, Corrupted versions of elements for it's elementals(like sludge and balefire instead of normal earth and fire), spirits of specific destructive actions(like murder) and twisted reflections of normal emotions(like incest and rape instead of natural lust).<br /> <br /> Technically you could get a wolf of the wyrm though. The Wyrm has the ability to corrupt spirits of the wyld, weaver, and gaia to it's service(at the cost of turning them into twisted shells of their healthy siblings)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482610#post1482610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And another thing is that in the Umbra everything can be real as long as there is a counterpart in the physical world, so do you think there could be vampire spirits? They would probably be banes but is it something possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. There are specifically no spirit counterparts to humans, and above all vampires are human. You can have spirits of &quot;vampirism&quot; in the sense of draining life, but that would have as much to do with VTM vampires as the life-drain spell in skyrim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:44:33-07:00","id":1482629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482611#post1482611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No... er, mostly. Wolf spirits would be more Gaian than anything. The wyrm is the spiritual god of decay, destruction, and corruption, so spirits aligned to it would be things like fungi and parasites instead of normal plant/animal spirits</div> </div> </div> </div>Fungi and parasites are not some edgy alternative to &quot;normal plants and animals&quot;. Fungal superorganisms, in fact, are ubiquitous in the kind of forested terrain the Garou prefer, with 100+ tons of biomass (all from the same single fungus) spread out over a vast area to act as a kind of nutrient catch net. This keeps anything that keels over and dies from stinking up the place for an extended period of time, as the hyphae help to break down dead things faster and spare the rest of woods a monopoly of foul-smelling, potentially pathogenic bacterial blooms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:22:25-07:00","id":1482633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482629#post1482629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fungi and parasites are not some edgy alternative to &quot;normal plants and animals&quot;. Fungal superorganisms, in fact, are ubiquitous in the kind of forested terrain the Garou prefer, with 100+ tons of biomass (all from the same single fungus) spread out over a vast area to act as a kind of nutrient catch net. This keeps anything that keels over and dies from stinking up the place for an extended period of time, as the hyphae help to break down dead things faster and spare the rest of woods a monopoly of foul-smelling, potentially pathogenic bacterial blooms.</div> </div> </div> </div>They would still be Wyrm-aligned, though, as they're still linked to death and decay and that is Wyrm in WtA cosmology, although it can be said to be from the un-corrupted Wyrm, which is still an existing notion in the setting. How much those spirits became corrupted or are still linked to the corrupted Wyrm depends on your personal interpretation of WtA'a cosmology when we get to its most gonzo and ill-conceived designs.<br /> <br /> But yes, they're not &quot;edgy corruptions&quot; of plants and animals and aren't usually considered so even in the setting. Werewolves do not regularly go through the forest in mushroom-killing sprees in their war against the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T12:36:07-07:00","id":1482638,"title":"","content":"There's no counterpart for humans, but why? Wolves have one, trees have one, concept have one (in some case they can be found in other realm of Umbra but still) so why not humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:02:40-07:00","id":1482665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482629#post1482629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fungi and parasites are not some edgy alternative to &quot;normal plants and animals&quot;. Fungal superorganisms, in fact, are ubiquitous in the kind of forested terrain the Garou prefer, with 100+ tons of biomass (all from the same single fungus) spread out over a vast area to act as a kind of nutrient catch net. This keeps anything that keels over and dies from stinking up the place for an extended period of time, as the hyphae help to break down dead things faster and spare the rest of woods a monopoly of foul-smelling, potentially pathogenic bacterial blooms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I'm familiar with mycology. This is however a game about magic and fungi are symbolically associated with death, rot, poison, and disease.<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying they're edgy versions of plants and animals, I'm saying the wyrm would likely have these<i> Instead </i>of normal plants and animals normally(barring corrupted versions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482638#post1482638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no counterpart for humans, but why? Wolves have one, trees have one, concept have one (in some case they can be found in other realm of Umbra but still) so why not humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one is sure why It's kind of ironic for the WoD game that's thematically about realizing &quot;humanity isn't the center of the universe and needs to come to balance with nature to survive&quot; ends up making humans Extra-special anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:57:29-07:00","id":1482677,"title":"","content":"Humans\u2014and possibly dead humans reanimated by the vampiric curse\u2014have <i>souls</i>. Each one has, or had at one time, an individual spirit of its very own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:25:26-07:00","id":1482684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482665#post1482665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know, I'm familiar with mycology. This is however a game about magic and fungi are symbolically associated with death, rot, poison, and disease.<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying they're edgy versions of plants and animals, I'm saying the wyrm would likely have these<i> Instead </i>of normal plants and animals normally(barring corrupted versions).</div> </div> </div> </div>It really wouldn't, because that would promote too much health, at least as far as the fungi are concerned. What else can promote timely breakdowns of dead matter so that they can be recycled and also knock the teeth out of radiation in some cases? The establishment of &quot;fungi are Wyrmy&quot; is really a knee-jerk, early installment bit that can be chalked up to baggage from D&amp;D's mushroom men. Just as W:tA can adjust to getting new science in about hyenas, it can steer away from tarring fungi and parasites. Also worth noting that in spite of the association of cephalopods with Qyrl, there are still octopus-spirits that are Gaian. This isn't W:tF, the line isn't that cut and dry about weird associations with certain animals over others vis a vis the Hosts and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No one is sure why It's kind of ironic for the WoD game that's thematically about realizing &quot;humanity isn't the center of the universe and needs to come to balance with nature to survive&quot; ends up making humans Extra-special anyway. </div> </div> </div>It focuses on them as a part of werebeasts, but that doesn't necessarily make them special the way that Mage or Vampire see them as special. Humans are a component of the main characters of werewolf, one that plays host to a lot of errant individuals that are up to no good. What's more, while a Changing Breed can't survive the loss of its beast kin, it can survive the loss of its human-alike component, as the Mokole did (it was a long, long time between when the Kings died and when the Dragon Breed adopted human form). Humans are basically the less vital component there.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Vampire and Mage don't stop talking about humanity this, humanity that, and anything else is an afterthought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T17:48:14-07:00","id":1482688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really wouldn't, because that would promote too much health, at least as far as the fungi are concerned. What else can promote timely breakdowns of dead matter so that they can be recycled and also knock the teeth out of radiation in some cases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds Very wyrmy to me. It does it's job exclusively through the destruction and breakdown of other things. Even radiation is them using wyrm-essence to Eat another wyrm-tainted thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The establishment of &quot;fungi are Wyrmy&quot; is really a knee-jerk, early installment bit that can be chalked up to baggage from D&amp;D's mushroom men.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fungi have been associated with disease at least since the medieval and rot since time immemorial, so I'm not sure it's really Knee-jerk to say that when it's been part of popular culture for a While now. Like many things, D&amp;D just aped a popular concept, they didn't invent it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just as W:tA can adjust to getting new science in about hyenas, it can steer away from tarring fungi and parasites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern science has showed us that the Vast majority of fungal species(by both number of species and amount of biomass) are disease causing single-celled microbes and not mushrooms anyway, so it's not even inaccurate to real life.<br /> <br /> Fungi are primarily eating machines that occasionally have useful mutations and a small number of them have a fascinating bio-internet fueled resource economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting that in spite of the association of cephalopods with Qyrl, there are still octopus-spirits that are Gaian. This isn't W:tF, the line isn't that cut and dry about weird associations with certain animals over others vis a vis the Hosts and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure how that's relevant? Cepholopods aren't normally associated with wyrmy concepts like destruction and the Qyrl are a WoD invention<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It focuses on them as a part of werebeasts, but that doesn't necessarily make them special the way that Mage or Vampire see them as special. Humans are a component of the main characters of werewolf, one that plays host to a lot of errant individuals that are up to no good. What's more, while a Changing Breed can't survive the loss of its beast kin, it can survive the loss of its human-alike component, as the Mokole did (it was a long, long time between when the Kings died and when the Dragon Breed adopted human form). Humans are basically the less vital component there.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Vampire and Mage don't stop talking about humanity this, humanity that, and anything else is an afterthought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans are the only species without spirits and are given Souls instead. That makes them pretty special even outside of were-beast association. They may not be the central player of the game, but it also causes some thematic dissonance to say humans aren't special on one hand and then make them special on the other in a way that isn't necessary.<br /> <br /> What would be wrong with the idea of human spirits anyway? Why exclude them? Why make souls humanity-exclusive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-01-2022, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T07:25:59-07:00","id":1482748,"title":"","content":"The idea that human aren't special is what i like in Werewolf the Apocalypse, that's why on this game it should be fixed if the ST need it.<br /> Humans have intelligence yes but another being could have develop it in future or in different circonstances in past, that doesn't make them special.<br /> Werewolf the apocalypse is a game that tell that every life are the same, no one is above the other, so telling that humans does not have spirit but souls...<br /> Nah, not in that game, instant golden rule to fix it<br /> <br /> Including human spirits would be interesting in other way, in umbral city they could act and serve weaver purpose while in wild environnements they could act like predators as other wyld animal spirit<br /> Same spirit, different umbral purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:33:50-07:00","id":1482778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really wouldn't, because that would promote too much health, at least as far as the fungi are concerned. What else can promote timely breakdowns of dead matter so that they can be recycled and also knock the teeth out of radiation in some cases? The establishment of &quot;fungi are Wyrmy&quot; is really a knee-jerk, early installment bit that can be chalked up to baggage from D&amp;D's mushroom men. Just as W:tA can adjust to getting new science in about hyenas, it can steer away from tarring fungi and parasites. Also worth noting that in spite of the association of cephalopods with Qyrl, there are still octopus-spirits that are Gaian. This isn't W:tF, the line isn't that cut and dry about weird associations with certain animals over others vis a vis the Hosts and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, with time the game adjusted to get new science about the Wyrm, too.<br /> <br /> While you're completely right if we assume the Wyrm only in its current, corrupted iteration, the Wyrm isn't mainly about corruption. It is mainly about destruction, sudden or gradual, and decay, which are completely natural, healthy and necessary processes. In the Triatic cosmology of Werewolf you really don't have a good reason to associate those spirits to the other two: fungi and parasites promote growth and order as aftereffects, but their direct action is promoting the decay of other organisms.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can have any particular spirit belong to any given &quot;class&quot; for any number of reasons, and you may have most such spirits having &quot;switched sides&quot; in the past to avoid corruption. But if the only reason to avoid linking them to the Wyrm is its corruption, it won't change that they're originally Wyrm spirits, that they're the most likely to represent the concept of still uncorrupted Wyrm Spirits, and the matter at hand: that the Wyrm would favor such &quot;plant/animal&quot; spirits over other, regardless if the majority of those spirits are Tainted, because this assertion isn't about the majority of Fungi spirits, but about the majority of Wyrm spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482684#post1482684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It focuses on them as a part of werebeasts, but that doesn't necessarily make them special the way that Mage or Vampire see them as special. Humans are a component of the main characters of werewolf, one that plays host to a lot of errant individuals that are up to no good. What's more, while a Changing Breed can't survive the loss of its beast kin, it can survive the loss of its human-alike component, as the Mokole did (it was a long, long time between when the Kings died and when the Dragon Breed adopted human form). Humans are basically the less vital component there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being able to justify it by the lore doesn't change the irony observed. While Werewolf is about humans not being special for all the reasons you pointed, it still makes humans special in practical terms, both by making them have ghosts instead of spirits and by making them the singular common trait among all the Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Even, by the way, Breeds that loath humans from the bottom of their hearts. We're <u>told</u> that humans are the least relevant aspect of the equation, but we're never given direct evidence. All Breeds use humans, no one ever shown the possibility of changing that. Or better, a few did: Pentex's artificial Breeds include one or two without any human side, but I hardly think they're a good evidence that this is along the natural way of things.<br /> <br /> This is just irony. The game is meant to tell stories about wolf-men to and by human players, and it came out in the early 90's, there's no need to take those facts seriously if you don't want to, the game is clearly meant to be serious about humans not being special. But it is an option for any ST or group that wants to play humans as being special, without actually breaking the setting since we only have the Changers word for it, so unreliable narrator and all that. It is also relevant because the settings are distinct but meant to reference each other, so Werewolf can't really <u>prove</u> humans aren't a big deal to not break the already tenuous connection with other lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:41:35-07:00","id":1482781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482748#post1482748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including human spirits would be interesting in other way, in umbral city they could act and serve weaver purpose while in wild environnements they could act like predators as other wyld animal spirit<br /> Same spirit, different umbral purpose</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all: I like the idea, it's neat and I'm all in favor of changing bits of the setting to further enshrine each game on its themes and as the center of its own setting.<br /> <br /> That said, though, this isn't strictly necessary. Humans being &quot;special may come from some interference by a third party, Maybe the Weaver or the Wyrm created the Dark Umbra in a bid to make those apes into a specialized tool for their goals or something, or maybe someone else interfered.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Maybe even this is always the state of the current &quot;dominant&quot; species in the globe, for whatever measure of &quot;dominant&quot; you want to take. It could even be fun to have the cosmology suddenly shift under our feet to make Ravens or Octopuses into the new Metaphysical Dominant Species for reasons we can only guess. Like, not retcon, but shift in the middle of the year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 06-02-2022, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T03:57:08-07:00","id":1482918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1482781#post1482781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">changing bits of the setting to further enshrine each game on its themes and as the center of its own setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something i saw on other tables, in some game they add the ability to turn humans into werewolf by biting them at the condition to have at least 3 in &quot;Primal Urge&quot; and resist frenezy when biting cause of the blood taste which excites the predator's instinct of werewolf, and the bite can turn only in Crinos and hispo form so impossible to avoid frenezy roll<br /> To explain why Black Spiral dancer weren't using this ability the ST statued that Ga\u00efa cursed them to be incapable of spreading the wolf blood that way, same for wyrm corrupted werewolves.<br /> The auspice was defined by the main character trait of the bitten person, his tribes was define through a ritual of integration and Werewolves can only turn Humans or Wolves that way.<br /> <br /> Also he was telling that garou must chose human that was worthy to avoid changing a wyrm tainted man and creating another ennemy<br /> <br /> I didn't include that in my game but it looks pretty well thought out for Werewolf the Apocalypse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-12T03:39:34-07:00","id":1483782,"title":"","content":"I've always ran things in a way that everything needs the Wyld, the Weaver and the Wyrm to work correctly. And still, the Wyrm performs many things that are needed for life to carry on and Gaia to nurture all the life upon her. Death is natural and a part of this lifecycle, fungi and similar things that we might find creepy and crawly are outside our experience and make us uncomfortable. Fundamentally, I feel that we need to underscore the fact that the experience of Gaia and the ecology of Gaia Garou fight to preserve is way more complicated than what humans feel is likeable.<br /> <br /> For this reason I can completely see fungi being normal Gaian spirits and doing Gaian stuff. There are many Gaian things corrupted by the (mad) Wyrm and surely there is room to create horrifying monstrosities based on fungi if you want them. I've applied the same logic to Qyrl. There are many molluscs in the sea that are of Gaia, and there are spirits representing them that are still clear oft the madness. I think there are great opportunities to actually protect these from overzealous Garou/Rokea or the Corrupted version seeking to bring more of them into the (Mad) Wyrm's embrace.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-17T10:54:17-07:00","id":1484293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1483782#post1483782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always ran things in a way that everything needs the Wyld, the Weaver and the Wyrm to work correctly. And still, the Wyrm performs many things that are needed for life to carry on and Gaia to nurture all the life upon her. Death is natural and a part of this lifecycle, fungi and similar things that we might find creepy and crawly are outside our experience and make us uncomfortable. Fundamentally, I feel that we need to underscore the fact that the experience of Gaia and the ecology of Gaia Garou fight to preserve is way more complicated than what humans feel is likeable.<br /> <br /> For this reason I can completely see fungi being normal Gaian spirits and doing Gaian stuff. There are many Gaian things corrupted by the (mad) Wyrm and surely there is room to create horrifying monstrosities based on fungi if you want them. I've applied the same logic to Qyrl. There are many molluscs in the sea that are of Gaia, and there are spirits representing them that are still clear oft the madness. I think there are great opportunities to actually protect these from overzealous Garou/Rokea or the Corrupted version seeking to bring more of them into the (Mad) Wyrm's embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being of gaia and being of the wyrm are not mutually exclusive unless we're talking about the possessed(because gaian spirits don't create kami, pieces of Gaia do).<br /> <br /> You can have things that are wyrmish and still have them smell of gaia as well, as they'd be things that are of the wyrm in it's capacity as the balance-bringer.There should honestly still be plenty of those things around, because the wyrm never Stopped doing it's gaian given duties, it just added a side-job of also being a corruptive influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T03:20:04-07:00","id":1484344,"title":"","content":"Well there isn't a Sense Gaia, and most spirits belonging to the Wyrm are actually corrupted spirits of other types (including a LOT of Gaian Spirits). Heck my example is that mollusc spirits would be Gaian spirits by default and only some of them would be Wyrm corrupted. I also state in the beginning that Wyrm does most of its job as it should. So I really don't get your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T16:52:54-07:00","id":1484398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484344#post1484344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there isn't a Sense Gaia, and most spirits belonging to the Wyrm are actually corrupted spirits of other types (including a LOT of Gaian Spirits). Heck my example is that mollusc spirits would be Gaian spirits by default and only some of them would be Wyrm corrupted. I also state in the beginning that Wyrm does most of its job as it should. So I really don't get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all wyrm spirits are &quot;corrupted&quot; or Evil. Some are quite literally spirits that spawn as &quot;of the wyrm's brood&quot; similar to how pattern spiders are firmly weaver-spirits. Some wyrm spirits can be both team wyrm and team gaia At The Same Time, because they're wyrmish spirits doing what the wyrm is intended to do.<br /> <br /> That's my point, spirits aren't necessarily binary creatures that are only on one team at a time(many of the incarna in canon are even kind of split in their loyalties). So a Fungi would be a wyrm spirit, that would smell of the wyrm and be 100% wyrmish brood, but Also a gaian spirit because it's doing it's gaia-ordained job of keeping balance.<br /> <br /> The thing I'm disagreeing with was that fungi are &quot;normal gaian spirits&quot; that need to be corrupted by the wyrm to be part of the wyrmish brood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-18T22:21:09-07:00","id":1484415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484398#post1484398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all wyrm spirits are &quot;corrupted&quot; or Evil. Some are quite literally spirits that spawn as &quot;of the wyrm's brood&quot; similar to how pattern spiders are firmly weaver-spirits. Some wyrm spirits can be both team wyrm and team gaia At The Same Time, because they're wyrmish spirits doing what the wyrm is intended to do.<br /> <br /> That's my point, spirits aren't necessarily binary creatures that are only on one team at a time(many of the incarna in canon are even kind of split in their loyalties). So a Fungi would be a wyrm spirit, that would smell of the wyrm and be 100% wyrmish brood, but Also a gaian spirit because it's doing it's gaia-ordained job of keeping balance.<br /> <br /> The thing I'm disagreeing with was that fungi are &quot;normal gaian spirits&quot; that need to be corrupted by the wyrm to be part of the wyrmish brood.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wyrm-spirits that are doing the job that they're supposed to be doing are supposed to be super-rare. When one turns up, like the Great Serpent in Pangaea, it's a bit of a big deal. This presumably does not include every fungus spirit around every forest; they would almost certainly register as Gaian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T12:26:55-07:00","id":1484436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484415#post1484415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrm-spirits that are doing the job that they're supposed to be doing are supposed to be super-rare. When one turns up, like the Great Serpent in Pangaea, it's a bit of a big deal. This presumably does not include every fungus spirit around every forest; they would almost certainly register as Gaian.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of disagree with that. Fungi are 100% wyrmish, you cannot convince me otherwise.<br /> <br /> Joking aside, Nature doesn't work correctly unless there are A Lot of things that the wyrm is supposed to be in charge of are doing their job, in the sense that if they stopped the world would start looking apocalyptic within a year.<br /> <br /> Some of the bigger examples being death and entropy. If the former stopped then nature would turn into a realm of eternal starvation and torment as things would be unable to die or be digested. If the later stopped, the universe would freeze into a single moment of suspended time as nothing changed forever.<br /> <br /> Granted, that could probably be handwaved as &quot;Major Wyrm incarna who are still balanced oriented are a big deal, but minor spirits don't really count since they aren't sentient enough to be on anyone's sides&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-19-2022, 04:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T13:15:36-07:00","id":1484440,"title":"","content":"This is a difference in what the setting traditionally says versus what makes sense.<br /> <br /> \u200bI understand what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> means: no matter how much those spirits were originally Wyrmish, in the lore most of them cut ties with the Wyrm when the whole corruption debacle happened. So they're Gaian, but under no member of the Triat. It is less about what they represent and more about their active decision to take a side.<br /> <br /> On my part I know this, but I'm not completely <i>convinced</i> of its logic. But more importantly, in the context of the thread it has indeed more to do with the nature of those spirits than this decision, that is, their <i>original</i> link to the Wyrm explains why Vampires aren't necessarily linked to the corruption just because they're linked to the Wyrm, and the existence of rare non-cirrupt Wyrm spirits reinforces that.<br /> <br /> Vampires may very well be older than the Wyrm's corruption and actually occupy a natural niche modern werewolves just do not understand (as most of them also do not understand non-corrupt Wyrmish spirits, or even heard about them, yet they're a real thing). It may well be that the modern Beast is a development from after the Wyrm's fall and a consequence of it corrupting them, when high-Humanity/Path Vampires may be more free from this corruption.<br /> <br /> Golconda, in this sense, may very well be about freeing the vampire from the Tainting influence and accepting their Gaian niche, which would be a very interesting way to portray such vampires in a Werewolf game and add a lot of nuance that would be interesting in a game that seeks to explore contacts between the two from a Werewolf perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T15:20:01-07:00","id":1484445,"title":"","content":"I don't think that a thematic resonance to an activity that promotes balance makes one register on a Sense $TRIATIC_MEMBER, or else Garou would all be very confused about why they smell like the Wyrm for all of their efforts to stop the rampant cosmic forces arrayed against them and the ally of the moment, the Wyld.<br /> <br /> (It's a long moment.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-19T16:38:59-07:00","id":1484451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484445#post1484445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that a thematic resonance to an activity that promotes balance makes one register on a Sense $TRIATIC_MEMBER, or else Garou would all be very confused about why they smell like the Wyrm for all of their efforts to stop the rampant cosmic forces arrayed against them and the ally of the moment, the Wyld.<br /> <br /> (It's a long moment.)</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but the Wyrm being &quot;present&quot; doesn't mean it is an inherently unbalanced activity, either. Non-corrupted Wyrm spirits still register as Wyrm to this Sense, which is one of the complications that arise when the Garou find them, many ok things and situations still have a faint Wyrm &quot;smell&quot; to them, which is the explanation for Sense Wyrm not always working (it isn't about not sensing anything. but not accurately getting &quot;excessive Wyrm&quot; from normal, expected levels), and Humanity 7+ Vampires do not register as Wyrm despite still being Vampires.<br /> <br /> So while the Wyrm Smell on Humanity 6- vampires certainly means some resonance with the current Wyrm, it doesn't mean this taint is intrinsic or original to their state, it may be a later development. And again, Golconda requires precisely Humanity 7+, so in this state it is certain that the vampire shouldn't register as Wyrm-Tainted. And we wouldn't ever know if it registers as Gaian since there's no Sense Gaia;<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm not holding that this is in any way, shape or form intended as the official take in the setting. Just that it is a possible interpretation with the current Werewolf lore and could be interesting in some Werewolf games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T19:16:19-07:00","id":1484567,"title":"","content":"I think part of the confusion is because there is a heavy element of Christian and Humanist thought in how the corrupter Wyrm is presented, and that thought isn't really consistent with nature. Most human criminal behavior is considered Of The Wyrm by the books, yet animals commit acts that are deeply criminal all the time. Lions treat their females like slaves, and murder the children of other males, for example. Lions also kill the children of rival predators even when they are not hungry enough to eat them. Are lions Of The Wyrm?<br /> <br /> So what does &quot;corruption&quot; actually mean? Generally it is presented as a blend of those things a Christian, a Humanist, and a, for want of a better word, hippy would consider evil. Vampires are considered &quot;of the wyrm&quot; when below Humanity 7 because that's the level where they start routinely doing things that a blend of Christian, Humanist, and hippy thinking would consider evil. I really think the books themselves are written from that simplistic a way of thinking. Players twist ourselves into knots trying to add depth to what is rooted in a really safe, conventional, shallow mindset.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T10:58:52-07:00","id":1484624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484398#post1484398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all wyrm spirits are &quot;corrupted&quot; or Evil. Some are quite literally spirits that spawn as &quot;of the wyrm's brood&quot; similar to how pattern spiders are firmly weaver-spirits. Some wyrm spirits can be both team wyrm and team gaia At The Same Time, because they're wyrmish spirits doing what the wyrm is intended to do.<br /> <br /> That's my point, spirits aren't necessarily binary creatures that are only on one team at a time(many of the incarna in canon are even kind of split in their loyalties). So a Fungi would be a wyrm spirit, that would smell of the wyrm and be 100% wyrmish brood, but Also a gaian spirit because it's doing it's gaia-ordained job of keeping balance.<br /> <br /> The thing I'm disagreeing with was that fungi are &quot;normal gaian spirits&quot; that need to be corrupted by the wyrm to be part of the wyrmish brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I've stressed about half dozen times that there is a difference between corrupted Wyrmish influence and Wyrmish influence. It takes all of the Triat to create anything in the Tellurian. And Fungi are normal Gaian spirits since they are normal natural beings belonging to Earth and as such are part of her brood. That they serve in the role of the pure wyrm in their purpose is but a facet of existence and natural.<br /> <br /> As for spirits that are not corrupted, but are actual Wyrm spirits and not insane monsters, there's bound toa few going about on their merry way, even after the Wyrm tried reforming itself into the thing it is today. But as the Book of the Wyld says, there's way more to the Triat and their servants than what we see, if you ever did encounter one of those rarities they would register with Sense Wyrm, but as <i>something distinctly different</i>.<br /> <br /> The purpose of Sense Wyrm/Weaver/Wyld is not to measure the comparitive composition of elements of reality but to detect the influence of excessive outside corruption.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484567#post1484567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the confusion is because there is a heavy element of Christian and Humanist thought in how the corrupter Wyrm is presented, and that thought isn't really consistent with nature. Most human criminal behavior is considered Of The Wyrm by the books, yet animals commit acts that are deeply criminal all the time. Lions treat their females like slaves, and murder the children of other males, for example. Lions also kill the children of rival predators even when they are not hungry enough to eat them. Are lions Of The Wyrm?</div> </div> </div> </div>That may be western biases creeping into the game, rather than an error of the game itself. Wyrmish corruption is less defined by morality than it is by wanton destruction and debasement for the sake of debasement. Life happens, death happens. Wyrmish corruption happens when you take your time to be an asshole about it. If you steal you're not &quot;Of the Wyrm&quot;, if you stealing causes people to die you are. Heck, not even baseline capitalism is of the Wyrm, On a general basis soldier (or a Garou) won't stink of the Wyrm. A soldier who took his time raping a village and torturing people sure as hell will. Killing is not inherently Wyrmish, so your comparison with a Lion is quite moot. There is a moralist string to what &quot;Of the Wyrm&quot; means, but it is essentially based what is hurtful to Gaia's order, and that's a strange kind of morality compared to Christian values as it intentionally treats humans as just one part of the valuation of the world.<br /> <br /> I mean just looking at the classics of christianity, the Garou are pretty much ignoring all of them except &quot;Honor Thy Father&quot;. The rest is a shopping list which would shock anyone with actual Christian values. You have many Gods, some even treated above the main one by in setting groups, Graven imagery is pretty much the core way of participating in the religion, and taking what belongs to others is par course. Hippy values, they aren't either. Humanism... oh yes, they're all about compassion, justice and egalitarianism.<br /> <br /> Interestingly a lot of the ideas of fixing the world In Werewolf by certain groups are distinctly humanist, and I think that's a positive thing for the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:10:15-07:00","id":1484648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1482405-thoughts-about-the-bloody-man?p=1484624#post1484624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may be western biases creeping into the game, rather than an error of the game itself. Wyrmish corruption is less defined by morality than it is by wanton destruction and debasement for the sake of debasement. Life happens, death happens. Wyrmish corruption happens when you take your time to be an asshole about it. If you steal you're not &quot;Of the Wyrm&quot;, if you stealing causes people to die you are. Heck, not even baseline capitalism is of the Wyrm, On a general basis soldier (or a Garou) won't stink of the Wyrm. A soldier who took his time raping a village and torturing people sure as hell will.<b> Killing is not inherently Wyrmish</b>, so your comparison with a Lion is quite moot. There is a moralist string to what &quot;Of the Wyrm&quot; means, but it is essentially based what is hurtful to Gaia's order, and that's a strange kind of morality compared to Christian values as it intentionally treats humans as just one part of the valuation of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ifeel the highlighted point conflicts with all your previous points. Why would theft that results in death be wyrmish if killing is not inherently wyrmish? Why would there be a specific line about there being a clear and distinct difference between balance wyrm and hydra wyrm taint if, as per the reasoning you presented, balance wyrm taint would never manifest because only destruction that you &quot;you take your time to be an asshole about it&quot; manifests wyrm taint.<br /> <br /> This actually leads me to think in the opposite direction. Everything you listed <i>Would</i> be wyrmish, because it was an act of destruction(breaking a law for stealing, killing a person, breaking your word as a politician), but if it's not done in a corruptive manner it would probably carry Balance-wyrm taint rather than Hydra-wyrm taint(not that your average garou would tell the difference).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-21T14:59:19-07:00","id":1484655,"title":"","content":"I see no contradiction, for I know the narrative purpose of the Wyrm is as the antagonist and the narrative purpose of the Sense Gifts is in detecting corruption and complicating things because things can be corrupted while still being salvagable or not a threat to Gaia. The goal of the Wyrm is ultimate transformation, as it wanted to transform itself so it seeks to transform all. Yet it could not change its inherent nature as the balancer which is why the cosmos still lives and why basic functions of reality still are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}